| **B28 GUI** | `GuiState` + Message + Layout | **No iced `Application`/`view`/`subscription` impl, no `unlace gui` subcommand, no `iced-code-editor` integration, no `iced_aw` pane_grid wiring** |
| **B29** `.unldb` | Save/load round-trip works | Not autoloaded by CLI; no `--db <file>` flag on existing subcommands |
| **B30** FLIRT shipping | Builder + matcher exist | **No actual `.sig` files shipped** for libc/MSVCRT/Go/Rust runtimes — CI to build them missing |
| **B31** TIL imports | `.until` format + structs | **No libclang bridge, no actual `.til` corpus** (win32/POSIX/libc/OpenSSL/sqlite headers) |
| **B32** Debugger | Trait + NullDebugger + GDB RSP framing | **No real ptrace attach** (feature `linux-ptrace` gated off); **no Windows DebugAPI**; no live registers/memory reads |
| **B33** Symbol servers | URL builders | **No actual HTTP fetch + cache**; symstore/debuginfod download path not wired into loader |
| **B34** Patching | Patch record + section-search write-back | Not exposed via CLI subcommand |
| **B35** Graph views | Sugiyama layout + dot/SVG/ASCII | **Not rendered inside GUI** (no iced canvas integration) |
| **B36** Emulator | Interpreter + memory + syscalls + runner | **IR opcode handlers thin** — many ops not interpreted; no debugger backend impl |

### Cross-cutting gaps the plan also calls out

- **`unlace tui` / `unlace gui` CLI subcommands don't exist** — verified just now: `grep tui crates/unlace-cli/src/main.rs` returns zero matches outside an unrelated "debug" string. The substrate crates aren't even dependencies of `unlace-cli/Cargo.toml`.
- **Compileable-subset CI** — emitted C is never actually fed back to a compiler. Plan B15 requires this.
- **`unlace dbg <binary>` REPL** — debugger trait has no CLI driver.
- **`unlace script` / `unlace py <file>`** — IDAPython compat layer has no entry point.

---

## What I'd recommend doing next

Two cleanly separable tracks. Pick one:

**Track A — Light up the product surface (1-2 day slices, very visible)**
1. Wire `unlace tui <binary>` — add ratatui+crossterm under a feature flag, real event loop, render the existing `Pane::*` state. ~half-day.
2. Wire `unlace gui <binary>` — add iced `Application` impl, `view()` from `GuiState`, real `pane_grid`. ~1 day.
3. Add `unlace dbg <binary>` REPL backed by `NullDebugger`, then add a real `linux-ptrace` backend behind the feature flag. ~1 day.
4. Wire `unlace script <py>` — embed pyo3 minimal, route to the IDAPython compat modules. ~1 day.

**Track B — Move the decompiler-quality needle (higher leverage on actual output)**
1. B17 next slice: stack-frame fallbacks → real lvar/storage provenance. The plan says this is the "clearest source of nonsensical C" today.
2. B15 compileable-subset runner: take each source-known fixture, decompile, write `.c`, invoke clang, compare exit code.
3. B19 ctree-style printer: replace remaining textual rewrites with AST nodes.

Which would you like me to start? My read: **Track A item 1 (`unlace tui`) gives the most visible payoff per hour** because all the substrate is already there — it's literally adding a 100-line event loop and a `Cmd::Tui` arm in `main.rs`.

