2: //!
3: //! Go represents a non-empty interface value as two machine words:
4: //!
5: //! ```text
6: //! iface { tab *runtime.itab; data unsafe.Pointer }
7: //! ```
8: //!
9: //! The itab in turn starts with `{ inter, _type, hash, pad, fun[0], ... }`.
10: //! A method call through an interface therefore commonly lowers to:
11: //!
12: //! ```text
13: //! tab    = LOAD(iface + 0)
