29: /// Logical bucket a [`Pass`] belongs to.
30: ///
31: /// Phases are declared in **canonical execution order**: a well-formed
32: /// pipeline runs passes whose `phase()` is non-decreasing. Cross-phase
33: /// dependencies (e.g. type recovery feeding back into local optimization)
34: /// are handled by the outer fixed-point loop, not by re-ordering.
35: ///
36: /// Batch 10 slice 1 introduces this enum for organizational purposes
37: /// only — the runtime pass order is not changed by adding phase tags.
38: /// A unit test in this file pins the current pipeline as phase-monotonic
39: /// (modulo documented deviations) so future reorderings stay honest.
40: #[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, Hash, PartialOrd, Ord)]
41: pub enum PassPhase {
42:     /// Lifter-level cleanup that runs *before* canonical optimization
43:     /// (call-boundary copy-prop, redundant flag elim, algebraic simplify,
44:     /// prologue/junk-code stripping, noreturn detection).
45:     PreOpt,
46:     /// Intra-block / single-pass simplification: SCCP, copy-prop, DCE,
47:     /// constant-fold, dead-store/flag elim, condition/bool simplify,
48:     /// strength-reduce, IV-elim, idiom recognition.
49:     LocalOpt,
50:     /// Cross-block / whole-CFG analysis: GVN, CSE, LICM, global copy-prop,
51:     /// cross-block DSE, tail-call detection, indirect call/jump resolution.
52:     GlobalOpt,
53:     /// Type inference, constraint solving, struct/field detection,
54:     /// language-specific recovery (C++ vtables, Rust enums, Go ifaces,
55:     /// ObjC dispatch), calling-convention detection.
56:     TypeRecovery,
